//! The TWO-WAY half of the false-premise repair — including a vacuous
//! **soundness** theorem.
//!
//! The blanket iota hypothesis quantifies over every pre-pass `w` with no
//! constraint, while `iota_reduct_whc` builds its reduct from `kapp_args
//! wmajor`. A `w` returning an unrelated constructor application therefore fires
//! the rule with the wrong fields and emits a reduct the term does not reduce
//! to. The premise is false, and everything carrying it is vacuous.
//!
//! `wh3_hiota_repair.rs` fixed the three-way path. This is the two-way one, and
//! it is the more serious half: `def_eq_fuel_wh_sound` is the faithful
//! algorithm's **soundness**, not its completeness. A vacuous soundness theorem
//! is a worse thing to be carrying, and nothing in the gate suite could have
//! noticed — a theorem with a false premise has an impeccably empty axiom
//! closure.
//!
//! # Two families, and a trap in the naming
//!
//! The `par` chain takes
//! `wh e = some rr -> par_reduces_cd_star the_red_env e rr`; the `defeq` chain
//! takes `wh e = some rr -> DefEq e rr`.
//!
//! `def_eq_whnf_join_wh_hw` belongs to the **par** family despite its `_wh`
//! name, because both its legs route through the par loop. Assuming the name
//! determines the family gives it the wrong side condition.
//!
//! # Why the constraint is free
//!
//! `w` is chosen exactly once per family — at the loop — and there the required
//! proof is the `Nat.rec` induction hypothesis already in scope: `hw := ih`,
//! literally, up to one beta. 24 application sites updated across the eight
//! declarations; zero unconstrained binders survive.
//!
//! `DerivedProved`, empty axiom closures.

use crate::spec::error::SpecError;
use crate::spec::Specification;

impl Specification {
    /// The two-way soundness chain, over a constrained pre-pass.
    pub(super) fn add_wh_hiota_repair(&mut self) -> Result<(), SpecError> {
        self.add_recursive_def(
            SRC_REDUCE_APP_HEAD_WH_PAR_HW,
            "reduce_app_head_wh_par_hw: the application-head step reduces parallel-wise. Eight of nine head arms appeal to hiota; each now passes hw alongside wh, with the pre-pass CONSTRAINED to be par-sound. The blanket form quantifies over every pre-pass function with no constraint and is FALSE; this is the repair. DerivedProved, zero axiom_deps.",
        )?;
        self.add_recursive_def(
            SRC_REDUCE_ONCE_RED_WH_PAR_HW,
            "reduce_once_red_wh_par_hw: one faithful step is a par_reduces_cd_star reduction, with the pre-pass CONSTRAINED to be par-sound. The blanket form quantifies over every pre-pass function with no constraint and is FALSE; this is the repair. DerivedProved, zero axiom_deps.",
        )?;
        self.add_recursive_def(
            SRC_WHNF_FUEL_RED_WH_PAR_HW,
            "whnf_fuel_red_wh_par_hw: the whole two-way faithful loop is a par_reduces_cd_star reduction, over a constrained pre-pass. At the single site where the pre-pass is chosen, the required soundness proof is the Nat.rec induction hypothesis already in scope — hw := ih, literally, up to one beta. So the constraint costs nothing where it is used and excludes exactly the pre-passes that made the blanket form false. DerivedProved, zero axiom_deps.",
        )?;
        self.add_recursive_def(
            SRC_REDUCE_APP_HEAD_WH_DEFEQ_HW,
            "reduce_app_head_wh_defeq_hw: the application-head step is a DefEq, with the pre-pass CONSTRAINED to be DefEq-sound. The blanket form quantifies over every pre-pass function with no constraint and is FALSE; this is the repair. DerivedProved, zero axiom_deps.",
        )?;
        self.add_recursive_def(
            SRC_REDUCE_ONCE_RED_WH_DEFEQ_HW,
            "reduce_once_red_wh_defeq_hw: one faithful step is a DefEq, with the pre-pass CONSTRAINED to be DefEq-sound. The blanket form quantifies over every pre-pass function with no constraint and is FALSE; this is the repair. DerivedProved, zero axiom_deps.",
        )?;
        self.add_recursive_def(
            SRC_WHNF_FUEL_RED_WH_DEFEQ_HW,
            "whnf_fuel_red_wh_defeq_hw: the whole faithful loop is a DefEq, with the pre-pass CONSTRAINED to be DefEq-sound. The blanket form quantifies over every pre-pass function with no constraint and is FALSE; this is the repair. DerivedProved, zero axiom_deps.",
        )?;
        self.add_recursive_def(
            SRC_DEF_EQ_FUEL_WH_SOUND_HW,
            "def_eq_fuel_wh_sound_hw: SOUNDNESS of the faithful conversion algorithm, over a constrained pre-pass — and this is the more serious half of the repair. \\
\\
def_eq_fuel_wh_sound carries the blanket iota premise, which is FALSE, so the faithful algorithm's SOUNDNESS was vacuous — not merely its completeness. A false premise makes a theorem vacuous rather than unprovable, and its axiom closure stays impeccably empty, so nothing in the gate suite could have noticed. \\
\\
WAS: for EVERY pre-pass function whatsoever, if the pre-pass iota fires it is a DefEq — therefore def_eq_fuel_wh is sound. The antecedent is satisfiable at a pre-pass that returns an unrelated constructor application, where iota_reduct_whc emits a reduct built from the wrong constructor's fields, so the premise is false and the theorem said nothing. \\
\\
NOW: if the pre-pass is itself DefEq-sound, then acceptance implies DefEq. Still a hypothesis, but a satisfiable one, satisfied at the only instance the development has. DerivedProved, zero axiom_deps.",
        )?;
        self.add_recursive_def(
            SRC_DEF_EQ_WHNF_JOIN_WH_HW,
            "def_eq_whnf_join_wh_hw: joinability of the two faithful whnf results, over a constrained iota residual. \\
\\
Note it takes the PAR side condition, not the DefEq one, despite the _wh name: both its legs route through the par loop rather than the DefEq loop. A reader who assumed the name determined the family would give it the wrong side condition and it would fail to apply. DerivedProved, zero axiom_deps.",
        )?;
        Ok(())
    }
}

